  "details": "An important but currently missing tool for world creators is the ability to create audio listeners that can be used to broadcast audio heard by them to other sources. \n\nFor example, a microphone with speakers, or an in-world telephone. \n\nThe current work-around of using custom voice falloff ranges is clunky, and not ideal. It only works with player voice, and has a harsh directionality to it.\n\nIt would also be great if these audio listeners or sources had filters you could apply to them, to simulate phone calls, or radio compression.",
